& [Decision1SharedBoundary] selects a new pure crate
  + crate name is cantor_procedure_tool
  + cantor_procedure_tool depends on cantor_core, serde, and serde_json only
  + cantor_cli depends on cantor_procedure_tool and owns argument, stdin, file, stdout, stderr, and exit projection only
  + cantor_core remains the semantic procedure kernel and does not acquire process-adapter response types
  + future schema and provider-neutral projection modules may depend on cantor_procedure_tool without making cantor_core depend on them
  + dependency direction is cantor_core <- cantor_procedure_tool <- cantor_cli and future projections
  - never: introduce a dependency cycle or move provider, process I/O, service, network, persistence, model, or effect behavior into the pure crate

& [Decision2SchemaDependency] is assessed and slice separated
  + schemars 1.2.2 is already exact in Cargo.lock with checksum 687274d293b6cdc6e73e0fee520bf2049650090d7164f87672d212a3c530cf4a
  + schemars 1.2.2 is cached offline, requires Rust 1.74, exposes explicit Draft 2020-12 settings, and documents serde-attribute adaptation
  + schemars remains transitive through rmcp during I01 and is not promoted to a direct dependency by extraction
  + CPMS-I02 may add exact schemars 1.2.2 as a direct dependency only under its own claimed lock and conformance proof
  + jsonschema 0.49.2 is the preferred independent I03 validator candidate because it supports Draft 2020-12 and meta-schema validation and requires Rust 1.85, within the workspace Rust 1.96 profile
  + jsonschema must use default-features false because its defaults permit HTTP and file resolution; no direct dependency is authorized until exact offline resolution and dependency audit pass
  + [schemars_primary] is https://docs.rs/crate/schemars/1.2.2
  + [jsonschema_primary] is https://docs.rs/crate/jsonschema/0.49.2

& [Decision3ResourceLimits] sets profile 0.1 ceilings
  + maximum canonical document bytes is 4194304
  + maximum canonical bundle bytes is 16777216
  + maximum named definitions is 256, giving 2.94 times the measured 87-type starting closure
  + maximum resolved references is 4096
  + maximum schema-document nesting depth is 64
  + maximum aggregate object properties is 4096
  + maximum aggregate enum alternatives is 2048
  + maximum semantic residuals is 1024
  + maximum conformance cases is 4096 and maximum aggregate corpus bytes is 67108864
  + every counter is checked during traversal and fails closed before allocation growth beyond its ceiling
  + data-instance recursive depth is not authorized by these schema-document limits

& [Decision4InventoryAndGolden] is captured
  + exact named transport closure is 80 core types plus 7 shared-wrapper candidates
  + schema command stdout is 1218 bytes, one LF, exit 0, SHA256 e2955b0dbc2ea904fd5b777bfa272dd4155dc0f622a53cbf5a341949383d17af
  + missing command stdout is 416 bytes, one LF, exit 2, SHA256 6f4175a8215eaa87baae541df122b5f6dbdf1615488507685f6a91b854ec6d18
  + help command stdout is 480 bytes, one LF, exit 2, SHA256 cc54e92b48bc87b992efe5696658c2ddb084450a4591c2e5a4cbf4624fc23484
  + unknown join command stdout is 418 bytes, one LF, exit 2, SHA256 1e3070e035d8d3dcee06773dbaf954739121c391bf36fd4d8f913c135f34e56e
  + existing subprocess fixtures remain the oracle for parameterized prepare, run, verify, refusal, malformed, unknown-field, and oversized cases

& [RecursiveSchemaFinding] blocks CPMS-I02 activation
  + ProcedureValue is recursive through array, map, and record values and is reachable from every substantive operation family
  + formation profile 0.1 rejects recursive definitions unless a finite resolved representation is separately proven
  + I02 must choose and prove either bounded recursive references with local-only resolution and an explicit data-depth guard or a finite transport projection
  + I01 extraction does not generate, validate, or claim a canonical JSON Schema and is therefore not blocked by this later decision

& [ReadinessDisposition] is split
  + CPMS-I01 is ready for one exact extraction signature
  + CPMS-I02 remains blocked on recursive-schema policy and a separately claimed dependency change
  + CPMS-I03 remains blocked on I02 proof, exact offline validator resolution, and no-resolution configuration
  + CPMS-I04 and CPMS-I05 retain their canonical dependency order

